# Virtual environment
venv/
.venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Database (contains real student data — never commit this)
futo_feedback.db*
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backup/

# Trained sentiment model (regenerate locally with train_model.py)
model/

# Secrets — never commit real SMTP credentials
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.streamlit/.session_test.json

# NLTK downloaded data (re-downloaded via download_nltk_data.py)
nltk_data/

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
.vscode/
powershell.bat

# Test scratch. The suites in tests/ are committed on purpose — they are the
# regression gate — but nothing they generate is.
tests/__pycache__/
*.tmp
*.bak
tests/_last_run.txt

# Editor/agent worktrees. These hold a full but STALE copy of this same app
# inside the repository, which is not something to deploy: it would ship a
# second, out-of-date copy of every module, and the suites that walk the tree
# would report findings in a file that never runs.
#
# Seven suites carry `.kilo` in their skip lists because of this. That skip is
# the reason a stale duplicate can sit here without any suite failing, which is
# exactly why it must not be committed: an untracked directory is invisible in
# review, and this one is a whole second copy of the application.
.kilo/

# The department handbook. 15 MB, a CamScanner scan, and nothing in the app
# reads it at runtime — the teaching-staff list in `config.py` was transcribed
# from it by hand and committed. Committing it would add a megabyte-scale binary
# to every clone to serve no code.
Department Handbook.PDF

# One-shot local dev artefacts: run-all transcripts and the Streamlit boot log.
_streamlit.log
_streamlit_*.log

# Documentation is authored and built on this machine only. The PDF and its
# source are not part of the repository: they are a deliverable, not application
# code, and a ~1 MB binary in every clone is not worth carrying. Both are
# regenerated with `python build_documentation.py`.
FUTO_IFT_Smart_Feedback_System_Documentation.pdf
docs/
build_documentation.py
verify_pdf_layout.py
verify_pdf_contents.py
futo_doc_build/
